# Gimbal startup pose for the sim iris (loaded after gazebo-iris-gimbal.parm).
#
# ArduPilot's default mount mode is RC targeting (MNT1_DEFLT_MODE 3). With the
# SITL RC sticks centred that holds the middle of MNT1_PITCH_MIN..MAX
# (-135..45), i.e. pitch -45 deg: the camera stares at the ground in front of
# the drone and never sees the car, and relative_position_controller only
# starts commanding the gimbal after its first detection.
#
# Neutral mode instead holds MNT1_NEUTRAL_* (deg) from boot until the
# controller's first MAVLink pitch/yaw command takes over.
#
# Pitch -5: the camera's vertical FOV is only about +-13.4 deg (0.8 rad HFOV,
# 16:9). The car 20 m ahead spans about -1..+3 deg from the camera while the
# drone sits on the ground and is about -8.5 deg after takeoff to 3 m, so -5
# keeps it in frame for both. (-12 would cut the car's roof off while on the
# ground.) Keep gimbal_initial_pitch_deg in relative_position_controller equal
# to MNT1_NEUTRAL_Y.
#
# If a change here seems to have no effect, SITL is using a value saved in
# ~/ardupilot/eeprom.bin: start sim_vehicle.py once with -w to wipe it.

MNT1_DEFLT_MODE  1
MNT1_NEUTRAL_X   0
MNT1_NEUTRAL_Y   -5
MNT1_NEUTRAL_Z   0
